+description: "Turns your own agent history into a comic (Hermes, Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode or any JSONL log). It reads your sessions, tool calls and kanban cards read-only, finds a story with a problem, a struggle and a result, and writes a chapter script where every line and caption carries the ids of the messages that state it — a claim the cited messages do not support is refused, not printed. A series ledger remembers what each chapter told, carries one open thread into the next, and refuses repeats; an idea deck of 16.9 billion frames keeps each chapter's world, villain and genre different. It then draws the episode with your own image route (your harness's image tool, a local ComfyUI, or your own API key) in one of 55 art styles, letters it with SIL OFL fonts, and exports pages, panels, X/LinkedIn/Discord sizes and a PDF. Disclosure — reads your Hermes history read-only (no file created, renamed, truncated or deleted, proven with strace in scripts/readonly_proof.sh), reads only the profile it runs as unless --all-profiles is given, redacts deterministically by default (the local model redaction pass is opt-in via --llm-url), and sends redacted text to Hermes's own model for writing and truth checks, and panel prompts to the image route you choose; writes plans, renders, a series ledger and character kits under the plugin data directory; no telemetry, no auto-posting, and no key at all is needed for the host or ComfyUI routes."
