+name: hermes-colab
+repo: https://github.com/PietrangeloManco/hermes-colab
+sha: f05cf934fff3b446f2e00cc32e19432e9e41e87b
+description: "Run Python scripts and Jupyter notebooks on Google Colab GPUs (T4 free tier, L4, A100, H100, TPU) from chat: Hermes assigns the runtime, uploads the code, keeps it alive, streams progress and GPU use, syncs outputs and checkpoints home while the job runs, resumes on a fresh runtime from the last checkpoint when Colab reclaims one, and reports back to the chat that started it; a Desktop page shows live runs with cancel and resume. Disclosure — needs the user's own Google Cloud OAuth client (Desktop app, Colaboratory scope) signed in with hermes auth add hermes-colab:google; Hermes attaches the token to colab.research.google.com only. Uploads the run's files (hidden files and folders, symlinks, hard links, virtualenvs and common credential files excluded; the home directory, HERMES_HOME and credential folders are refused as code or output folders) to the user's Colab runtime and executes them there with a small stdlib runner that pip-installs the run's requirements; runtimes consume the account's Colab compute units and are released when a run ends; a daemon thread supervises active runs (one per profile, lease-protected; with no active run it only reads the run store every 30 s); run records live in the profile's plugin data directory; a pre_llm_call hook adds a finished run's one-line summary to the starting chat's next turn."
+maintainer: PietrangeloManco
+tier: community
+category: tools
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22.7"
